      "premise_index": 0,
      "exact_statement": "Let k be a field, X a quasi-compact separated k-scheme, and F a quasi-coherent sheaf. A finite affine open cover and its affine finite intersections compute H^i(X,F) by the Čech complex. For every field extension k'/k and every i≥0, H^i(X_{k'},F_{k'}) is naturally H^i(X,F)⊗_k k'.",
